A||||6||isthiswhereiputausername?||testing headlight relays?||||1||
Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-09-2001||10:54 AM||||Is there anyway to test headlight relays to see if they are working?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||08-09-2001||12:21 PM||||Do either of your headlights work? If so check non functioning one on the good side. Another way is to get wiring schamitic and check your voltages. If neither one work replace the main relay on the drivers side.||||reg||1
Z||000002||LivoniaFieroGT||08-09-2001||12:37 PM||||If you really want to scrimp.... you can take apart the relay and inspect the fine wiring for a break and resolder the wire.  Take the cover off and activate the system. Watch it work.  I fixed mine that way once.<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000003||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-09-2001||03:08 PM||||Thanks.. Neither of the headlights work,  I took the motors off and both of them work. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||08-09-2001||03:58 PM||||Check the main relay, drivers side.<BR>Also check the fuse links for 12 volts located inside the trunk left side, front. Both are red.||||reg||1
Z||000005||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-09-2001||05:01 PM||||I tried another main relay, took the cover off it, no power going through it.. even when I crossed it, I also checked the wires going to the main relay, no live wires in any of them, (headlights on or off), I think I might give up on it and wire them up direct again..  Anyone know of a  good toggle type of switch that will work for the headlights? (one way for up,one for down then the middle for dead)?<P>Thanks<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jake_Dragon||08-09-2001||05:45 PM||||I always wondered why they put the relays up front where they get moisture from the road.<BR>Why not locate them back in the sealed part of the front compartment?<BR>My head lights don't work now, the motors are good I have had them out and can make them work but the relays are shot. One side will go up and both will go down but they don't stop running when the hit bottom. <BR>I have them unplugged for now but plan on relocating every thing back inside the sealed area.<BR>Another fall project.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://web.tampabay.rr.com/jakedragon" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/logo.gif">   </A>||||reg||5
